  "docs": {
    "lessons": [
      "2026-09-06: Harness UI \u2014 map is the board. Slim header. No dual doc dump. Desktop+mobile one ship.",
      "`locks_outrank` Disk LESSONS outrank chat dest. Baja recut without playable/LESSONS.md = fail. Extra ribbon hulls = fail",
      "`one_crew` Build / Bot / OpenClaw / Gemma / Qwen are one ladder. Not silos. Twin loads OPERATING-PROFILE.",
      "`crew_contract` Every pack injects CREW.md. Handoff refuses if CREW.md missing. He is the system; seats are his hands.",
      "Context: Christopher \u2014 game adjustments drop old locks and revive mistakes; system feels compartmentalized.",
      "Lesson: Locks on disk outrank chat impulse. Build/Grok/OpenClaw/Gemma/Qwen are one ladder, not silos.",
      "Do instead: Before game/Baja/harness edit \u2014 read LESSONS+PASS. Rebuild harness accurate to live state.json then improve ",
      "`oc_learn` logged by log-job."
    ],
    "principles": [
      "Hash moved or it is a miss. Existing file \u2260 done.",
      "Pack = dest + NOW names + DEST-LOCKS + lessons \u226420 + job. Encyclopedia = refuse.",
      "Do not invent dests. Park Law: A Baja \u00b7 B Twin \u00b7 C Paper. First is always-on \u2014 the before/after gate to MASTER, not a de",
      "Projects taxonomy is `projects/` (ACTIVE + PARKED windows). Dest SoT does not move.",
      "Disk locks outrank chat. Recuts that drop old rules and revive mistakes are a fail.",
      "Fail closed. Pack refuse, 402, or review refuse = no send.",
      "Twin is ask.py. Household never Grok Bot. Baja is Grok Build only.",
      "iMessage is the only human socket \u2014 in and out, through OpenClaw. One node.",
      "Less dumb \u2192 delete \u2192 simplify \u2192 accelerate \u2192 automate last.",
      "Ladder: script > Gemma 12b > Qwen 27b > Grok Build > Grok Bot.",
      "0 new Grok Bots. Swarm = existing OpenClaw seats sequenced by host `crew-seq.py`. Cloud deny except Bot stamp.",
      "Grok Build and Grok Bot are one conductor pair. After ship: one MASTER line. Next pack reads the tail."
    ],
    "lessons_n": 21,
    "principles_file": true,
    "lessons_file": true
  },
